## Laser treatment

For many people with open angle glaucoma or high eye pressure, NICE recommends **selective laser trabeculoplasty (SLT)** as the first treatment. It is a quick, painless laser that helps fluid drain from the eye. It may mean you do not need eye drops, or need fewer.

## Eye drops

Drops such as **latanoprost** lower eye pressure. They must be used **every day, usually for life**, even though you will not notice a difference.

- wash your hands, tilt your head back and pull down your lower eyelid
- press gently on the inner corner of your eye for a minute afterwards
- leave 5 minutes between different drops
- ask your pharmacist about an **eye drop aid** if you find it hard

## Surgery

If drops and laser do not control the pressure, you may be offered surgery, such as a **trabeculectomy**, to create a new drainage channel.

## Regular checks

You will have regular checks at the eye clinic for life to make sure treatment is working.
